      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:neutron_star_forge",
      "title": "Neutron Star Forge",
      "text": "Recreates the crushing interior of a collapsed star: neutronium, metallic hydrogen and quark matter. Each one a state of matter no lab on Earth has held.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 4$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Note to self: this controller is too complex for a crafting grid. It has to be built on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts before ordering anything."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Why it matters: a neutron star packs more than a Sun's mass into a city-sized sphere. Gravity crushes electrons into protons, leaving neutrons held up only by degeneracy pressure. Deeper in, neutrons may dissolve into free quarks. A teaspoon would weigh about a billion tonnes."
    },
